  "name": "Question 18",
  "problem": "What is the projection of the intersection between the sphere ${x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2}+(z+1)^{2}=36$ and the plane $z=3$ onto the $xy$-plane.",
  "worked_solution": "To find the intersection of the sphere and the plane $z=3$, we substitute $z=3$ into the equation of the sphere:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2}+(3+1)^{2} & =36 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2}+16 & =36 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & =20 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & =(2\\sqrt{5})^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nProjecting this onto the $xy$-plane gives us the equation of the circle of radius $2\\sqrt{5}$ centered at $(0,2).$",
